text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a Goblin.\\nGoblin Grenade deals 5 damage to any target.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Sacred Mesa unless you sacrifice a Pegasus.\\n{1}{W}: Create a 1/1 white Pegasus creature token with flying.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, target non-Wall creature an opponent controls gains forestwalk until your next upkeep. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Buyback—Sacrifice a land. (You may sacrifice a land in addition to any other costs as you cast this spell. If you do, put this card into your hand as it resolves.)\\nCreate a 1/1 white Pegasus creature token with flying.', 'Create X 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', 'Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control get +3/+3 and gain trample until end of turn.', 'Defender', 'Destroy all lands.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', "Destroy target nonartifact, nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Drifting Meadow enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+1.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +4/+0.', 'Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.', 'First strike', "First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)\\nProtection from black (This creature can't be blocked, targeted, dealt damage, or enchanted by anything black.)", "First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)\\nProtection from white (This creature can't be blocked, targeted, dealt damage, or enchanted by anything white.)", "First strike, forestwalk, vigilance (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike, it can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest, and attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)", 'First strike\\n{G}: Regenerate Ranger en-Vec.', 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nFirst strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nFirst strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)", 'Flying, haste', 'Flying, protection from red', 'Flying, vigilance', "Flying\\nAesthir Glider can't block.", 'Flying\\nWhenever Hypnotic Specter deals damage to an opponent, that player discards a card at random.', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', 'Hurricane deals X damage to each creature with flying and each player.', 'Icatian Javelineers enters the battlefield with a javelin counter on it.\\n{T}, Remove a javelin counter from Icatian Javelineers: It deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Lightning Bolt deals 3 damage to any target.', "Mogg Flunkies can't attack or block alone.", "Nevinyrral's Disk enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{1}, {T}: Destroy all artifacts, creatures, and enchantments.", 'Other Goblins get +1/+1 and have mountainwalk.', 'Polluted Mire enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Protection from black\\n{W}: Order of the White Shield gains first strike until end of turn.\\n{W}{W}: Order of the White Shield gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Protection from white', 'Protection from white\\n{B}: Knight of Stromgald gains first strike until end of turn.\\n{B}{B}: Knight of Stromgald gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Pyrotechnics deals 4 damage divided as you choose among any number of targets.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nWhenever Woolly Spider blocks a creature with flying, Woolly Spider gets +0/+2 until end of turn.', 'Sacrifice Mogg Fanatic: It deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Sacrifice a Goblin: Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Serrated Arrows enters the battlefield with three arrowhead counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if there are no arrowhead counters on Serrated Arrows, sacrifice it.\\n{T}, Remove an arrowhead counter from Serrated Arrows: Put a -1/-1 counter on target creature.', 'Slippery Karst enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Smoldering Crater enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target player discards two cards at random.', 'This spell costs {1} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nFireball deals X damage divided evenly, rounded down, among any number of targets.', "Trample\\nGoblin Mutant can't attack if defending player controls an untapped creature with power 3 or greater.\\nGoblin Mutant can't block creatures with power 3 or greater.", 'When Goblin Matron enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a Goblin card, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Goblin Recruiter enters the battlefield, search your library for any number of Goblin cards, reveal them, then shuffle and put those cards on top in any order.', "Whenever Goblin Snowman blocks, prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by it this turn.\\n{T}: Goblin Snowman deals 1 damage to target creature it's blocking.", "Whenever Goblin Vandal attacks and isn't blocked, you may pay {R}. If you do, destroy target artifact defending player controls and Goblin Vandal assigns no combat damage this turn.", "Whenever Spectral Bears attacks, if defending player controls no black nontoken permanents, it doesn't untap during your next untap step.", "You may exile a red card from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nPyrokinesis deals 4 damage divided as you choose among any number of target creatures.", '{1}{G}: Regenerate Gorilla Chieftain.', '{1}{W}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{2}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{2}{R}, Sacrifice two Goblins: Create three 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', '{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Scavenger Folk: Destroy target artifact.', '{R}, {T}: Destroy target artifact. That artifact deals damage equal to its mana value to Goblin Tinkerer.', '{R}: Goblin Balloon Brigade gains flying until end of turn.', '{R}: Regenerate Uthden Troll.', '{T}, Sacrifice Goblin Digging Team: Destroy target Wall.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Strip Mine: Destroy target land.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}. Brushland deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Add {G}.\\n{T}: Target 1/1 creature gets +1/+2 until end of turn.', "{T}: Cuombajj Witches deals 1 damage to any target and 1 damage to any target of an opponent's choice.", '{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{T}: Target attacking creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.']
flavor: ['"A fine example of the rewards of artifice: a thoroughly obedient steed with wings of Soldevi steel."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi machinist', '"Battle doesn\'t need a purpose; the battle is its own purpose. You don\'t ask why a plague spreads or a field burns. Don\'t ask why I fight."', '"Can they *do* that?"\\n—Imwita, Zhalfirin artificer, last words', '"Could there be a fouler act? No doubt the baron knows of one."\\n—Autumn Willow', '"Do not go there, do not go / unless you rise on wings, unless you walk on hooves."\\n—"Song to the Sun," Femeref song', '"From down here we can make the whole wall collapse!"\\n"Uh, yeah, boss, but how do we get out?"', '"From up here we can drop rocks and arrows and more rocks!"\\n"Uh, yeah boss, but how do we get down?"', '"Goblins bred underground, their numbers hidden from the enemy until it was too late."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires*, vol. IV', '"Hi! ni! ya! Behold the man of flint, that\'s me! / Four lightnings zigzag from me, strike and return."\\n—Navajo war chant', '"I do not remember what he said to her. I remember her fiery eyes, fixed upon him for an instant. I remember a flash, and the hot breath of sudden flames made me turn away. When I looked again, Angus was gone."\\n—A wayfarer, on meeting Lady Orca', '"I don\'t suppose we could teach them to throw the cursed things?"\\n—Ivra Jursdotter', '"I got it! I got it! I—"', '"I hear there are Bears—or spirits—that guard caravans passing through the forest."\\n—Gulsen, abbey matron', '"Ihsan, the weak. Ihsan, the fallen. Ihsan, the betrayer. He has brought shame to the Serra Paladins where none existed before. May his suffering equal his betrayal."\\n—Baris, Serra Inquisitor', '"It had a mouth like that of a great beast, and gnashed its teeth as it strained to reach us. I am thankful it possessed no means of locomotion."\\n—Vervamon the Elder', '"Let no child be without a sword. We will all fight, for if we fail, we will certainly all die."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"Next!"', '"Oh, no—not *you* again?!"\\n—Jaya Ballard, task mage', '"Oi oi oi, me gotta hurt in \'ere,\\nOi oi oi, me smell a ting is near,\\nGonna bosh \'n gonna nosh\\n\'n da hurt\'ll disappear."\\n—Troll chant', '"Strength in numbers? Right."\\n—Ib Halfheart, goblin tactician', '"That does it! I\'m going back to hunting chickens!"\\n—Rhirhok, goblin archer', '"The clouds came alive and dove to the earth! Hooves flashed among the dark army, who fled before the spectacle of fury."\\n—*Song of All*, canto 211', '"The path of least resistance will seldom lead you beyond your doorstep."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"The raging winds . . . , settling on the sea, the surges sweep, / Raise liquid mountains, and disclose the deep."\\n—Virgil, *Aeneid*, Book I, trans. Dryden', '"The true dishonor for a soldier is surviving the war."\\n—Telim\'Tor', '"We are to be bound together as the reeds of a basket."\\n—Asmira, Rashida, and Jabari, unity chant', '"We called them \'armored lightning.\'"\\n—Gerrard of the *Weatherlight*', '"We know our place in the cycle of life—and it is not as flies."\\n—Eladamri, Lord of Leaves', '"We need not fear the forces of the air; I\'ve yet to see a Spider without an appetite."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, elvish hunter', '"When you\'re a goblin, you don\'t have to step forward to be a hero—everyone else just has to step back!"\\n—Biggum Flodrot, goblin veteran', '"Without Combat Medics, Icatia would probably not have withstood the forces of chaos as long as it did."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires*, vol. VI', '"You want to know your enemy? Look at your feet while you trample him."\\n—Tahngarth of the Weatherlight', 'A shield of light admits no shadow.', 'Asked how it survived a run-in with a bog imp, the pegasus just shook its mane and burped.', 'Born with wings of light and a sword of faith, this heavenly incarnation embodies both fury and purity.', 'Charging alone takes uncommong daring or uncommon stupidity. Or both.', 'For the first time in his life, Grakk felt a little warm and fuzzy inside.', 'Healers ultimately acquire the divine gifts of spiritual and physical wholeness. The most devout are also granted the ability to pass physical wholeness on to others.', 'One bone broken for every twig snapped underfoot.\\n—Llanowar penalty for trespassing', 'Out of the blackness and stench of the engulfing swamp emerged a shimmering figure. Only the splattered armor and ichor-stained sword hinted at the unfathomable evil the knight had just laid waste.', 'Speed and fire are always a deadly combination.', 'String, weapons, wax, or jewels—it makes no difference. Leave nothing unguarded in Scarwood.', 'The evisceration of one mogg always cheers up the rest.', 'They certainly are.', "They'll attack whatever's in front of them—as long as you tell them where that is.", "This timeworn relic was responsible for many of Urza's victories, though he never fully comprehended its mystic runes.", 'To be king, Numsgil did in Blog, who did in Unkful, who did in Viddle, who did in Loll, who did in Alrok . . . .', 'Unlike previous conflicts, the war between Urza and Mishra made Dominia itself a casualty of war.', "While it possesses potent venom, the giant spider often chooses not to paralyze its victims. Perhaps the creature enjoys the gentle rocking motion caused by its captives' struggles to escape its web."]
